The strongest direct triggers are Apple Watch and iPhone prompts for Pillow and SleepWatch, sound and snoring prompts for ShutEye and BetterSleep, and sleep-debt or broad sleep-improvement recommendations for Rise. Generic “best” questions can name several alternatives, while baby, toddler, apnea, Garmin, Samsung, ResMed, activity-tracker, and app-free prompts are less compatible with these five apps. The Oura queries may elicit Rise because it integrates with Oura, but they do not strongly point to the other four.

Top-down, I’d expect Pillow and SleepWatch to appear most often in this set because of its many Apple Watch prompts; ShutEye and BetterSleep to benefit from snoring and sound intent; and Rise to appear mostly in broad recommendation and Oura-related answers. Explicit mentions of Sleep Cycle in query wording could also prompt comparisons that name alternatives. Averaging estimated name mentions across all 100 questions, including criticism and comparisons, gives:

